      "id": "32a0430b-708c-402f-ad4a-31df7b11dad1",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 720,
        "content": "## SERP Rank Monitor powered by Bright Data\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule to monitor keyword rankings in Google SERP results. It reads tracked keywords from Google Sheets, queries Bright Data for search results, calculates the target domain's position, then writes the latest rank back to the sheet and sends a Slack notification.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger with the desired monitoring frequency.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the spreadsheet/range containing keywords and target domains.\n- Configure Bright Data credentials and SERP search settings for the desired Google locale, language, and device type.\n- Connect Slack credentials and choose the channel or recipient for rank update notifications.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the keyword sheet columns, target domain matching logic in the code node, SERP location/device parameters, and Slack message format to match the monitoring requirements."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "5959f95d-cf09-417f-a1a8-e51f36c5383f",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -48,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Load tracked keywords\n\nStarts the workflow on a schedule and retrieves the list of keywords to monitor from Google Sheets."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e8ec0559-7a83-4a9e-9b4a-3b3de2431694",
